  "requirements": [
    {
      "number": "1",
      "text": "Discuss with your counselor the influence that EIGHT of the following people or events had on the history of health care:",
      "children": [
        {
          "number": "1a",
          "text": "Hippocrates"
        },
        {
          "number": "1b",
          "text": "William Harvey"
        },
        {
          "number": "1c",
          "text": "Antoine van Leeuwenhoek"
        },
        {
          "number": "1d",
          "text": "Edward Jenner"
        },
        {
          "number": "1e",
          "text": "Florence Nightingale"
        },
        {
          "number": "1f",
          "text": "Louis Pasteur"
        },
        {
          "number": "1g",
          "text": "Gregor Mendel"
        },
        {
          "number": "1h",
          "text": "Joseph Lister"
        },
        {
          "number": "1i",
          "text": "Robert Koch"
        },
        {
          "number": "1j",
          "text": "Daniel Hale Williams"
        },
        {
          "number": "1k",
          "text": "Wilhelm Conrad Roentgen"
        },
        {
          "number": "1l",
          "text": "Marie and Pierre Curie"
        },
        {
          "number": "1m",
          "text": "Walter Reed"
        },
        {
          "number": "1n",
          "text": "Karl Landsteiner"
        },
        {
          "number": "1o",
          "text": "Alexander Fleming"
        },
        {
          "number": "1p",
          "text": "Charles Richard Drew"
        },
        {
          "number": "1q",
          "text": "Helen Taussig"
        },
        {
          "number": "1r",
          "text": "Jonas Salk"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "2",
      "text": "Explain the Hippocratic Oath to your counselor, and compare to the original version to a more modern one. Discuss to whom those subscribing to the original version of the oath owe the greatest allegiance."
    },
    {
      "number": "3",
      "text": "Discuss the health-care provider-patient relationship with your counselor, and the importance of such a relationship in the delivery of quality care to the patient. Describe the role of confidentiality in this relationship."
    },
    {
      "number": "4",
      "text": "Do the following:",
      "children": [
        {
          "number": "4a",
          "text": "Describe the roles the following people play in the delivery of health care.",
          "children": [
            {
              "number": "4a(1)",
              "text": "Allopathic physician (M.D.)and Osteopathic physician (D.O."
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(2)",
              "text": "Chiropractor (D.C.)"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(3)",
              "text": "Emergency medical technician"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(4)",
              "text": "Licensed practical/vocational nurse"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(5)",
              "text": "Medical assistant"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(6)",
              "text": "Medical laboratory technologist"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(7)",
              "text": "Nurse-midwife"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(8)",
              "text": "Nurse practitioner"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(9)",
              "text": "Occupational therapist"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(10)",
              "text": "Optometrist"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(11)",
              "text": "Pharmacist"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(12)",
              "text": "Physical therapist"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(13)",
              "text": "Physician's assistant"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(14)",
              "text": "Podiatrist"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(15)",
              "text": "Psychologist"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(16)",
              "text": "Radiologic technologist"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(17)",
              "text": "Registered Nurse"
            },
            {
              "number": "4a(18)",
              "text": "Respiratory therapist"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": "4b",
          "text": "Describe the educational and licensing requirements to practice health care in your state for FIVE of the professions in requirement 4a. (Not all professions may exist in your state.)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "5",
      "text": null,
      "children": [
        {
          "number": "5a",
          "text": "Tell what is meant by the term \"primary care\" with regard to a medical specialty."
        },
        {
          "number": "5b",
          "text": "Briefly describe the types of work done by physicians in the following specialties:",
          "children": [
            {
              "number": "5b(1)",
              "text": "Internal medicine*"
            },
            {
              "number": "5b(2)",
              "text": "Family practice*"
            },
            {
              "number": "5b(3)",
              "text": "Obstetrics/gynecology*"
            },
            {
              "number": "5b(4)",
              "text": "Pediatrics*"
            },
            {
              "number": "5b(5)",
              "text": "Psychiatry"
            },
            {
              "number": "5b(6)",
              "text": "Surgery"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": "5c",
          "text": "Describe the additional educational requirements for these specialties."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "6",
      "text": null,
      "children": [
        {
          "number": "6a",
          "text": "Briefly describe the types of work performed by physicians in FIVE of the following specialties or subspecialties:",
          "children": [
            {
              "number": "6a(1)",
              "text": "Allergy/immunology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(2)",
              "text": "Anesthesiology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(3)",
              "text": "Cardiology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(4)",
              "text": "Colorectal surgery"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(5)",
              "text": "Critical care medicine (intensive care medicine)"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(6)",
              "text": "Dermatology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(7)",
              "text": "Emergency Medicine"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(8)",
              "text": "Endocrinology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(9)",
              "text": "Gastroenterology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(10)",
              "text": "Geriatric medicine"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(11)",
              "text": "Hematology/oncology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(12)",
              "text": "Hospitalist"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(13)",
              "text": "Infectious disease"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(14)",
              "text": "Nephrology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(15)",
              "text": "Neuro surgery"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(16)",
              "text": "Neurology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(17)",
              "text": "Nuclear medicine"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(18)",
              "text": "Ophthalmology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(19)",
              "text": "Orthopedic surgery"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(20)",
              "text": "Otolaryngology/head and neck surgery"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(21)",
              "text": "Pathology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(22)",
              "text": "Physical medicine and rehabilitation"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(23)",
              "text": "Plastic, reconstructive, and maxillofacial surgery."
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(24)",
              "text": "Preventive medicine"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(25)",
              "text": "Pulmonology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(26)",
              "text": "Radiology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(27)",
              "text": "Rheumatology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(28)",
              "text": "Thoracic/cardiothoracic surgery"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(29)",
              "text": "Urology"
            },
            {
              "number": "6a(30)",
              "text": "Vascular surgery"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": "6b",
          "text": "Describe the additional educational requirements for the five specialties or subspecialties you chose in 6a."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "7",
      "text": null,
      "children": [
        {
          "number": "7a",
          "text": "Visit a physician's office,** preferably one who delivers \"primary care.\" (This may be that of your counselor.) Discuss the components of a medical history and physical examination (an official BSA health form may be used to guide this discussion), and become familiar with the instruments used."
        },
        {
          "number": "7b",
          "text": "Describe the characteristics of a good diagnostic test to screen for disease (e.g. routine blood pressure measurement). Explain briefly why diagnostic tests are not perfect."
        },
        {
          "number": "7c",
          "text": "Show how to take a blood pressure reading and a pulse reading."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "8",
      "text": "Do the following:",
      "children": [
        {
          "number": "8a",
          "text": "Discuss the roles medical societies, employers, the insurance industry, and the government play in influencing the practice of medicine in the United States."
        },
        {
          "number": "8b",
          "text": "Briefly tell how your state monitors the quality of health care within its borders, and how it provides care to those who do not have health insurance."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": "9",
      "text": "Compare and discuss with your counselor at least two types of health care delivery systems used throughout the world."
    },
    {
      "number": "10",
      "text": "Serve as a volunteer at a health-related event or facility in your community (e.g. blood drive, \"health fair\", blood pressure screening, etc.) approved by your counselor."
    }
  ],
